k County District Court\nRural Water\nSocial Sevice SWHHS\nSheriff Office\nTransfer Station\nUniversity Of Minnesota Extension Rock County\nVeterans Service Office\nLand Management Office\nJob Opportunities\nCommunity Links\nCommunity Services\nMinnesota Links\nTownship Officials\nCity Officials\nstart animation start slide 1 of 1\nAuditor Treasurer\nAshley Kurtz\nAuditor-Treasurer\nOpens in a new tab\n204 E. Brown Street\n507-283-5060\n507-283-1343\nashley.kurtz@rockmn.gov\nRock County Courthouse\nMonday - Friday\n8:00AM - 5:00PM\nRelated Pages\nTax Parcel Information\nRock County GIS\nProperty Taxes\nElections\nLicense Center\n2024 Financial Statement\nTax Capacity Rates\nUnderstanding Your Property Taxes\nAuctioneer License\nCity Officials\nTownship Officials\nVendor Payments\nAuditor Treasurer\nHome\nDepartment Directory\nAuditor Treasurer\nThe Rock County Auditor-Treasurer's Office is the accounting office of the County and is responsible for calculating, collecting and distributing taxes for the County, Cities, Township and School Districts. All monies are receipted and disbursed by this office. This office also calculates the county payroll and employee benefits; administers and maintains the election system; issues transient merchant, auctioneer and liquor licenses.\nFinance\nInvestments of County funds and interest collections\nAll receipt collections\nIssues warrants against all County funds\nMonthly financial reports\nYear-end financial report and 1099's\nAssists in annual audit\nCounty payroll preparation\nRegister of Bonds\nAssists with County Budget\nProperty Taxes\nFiling of all legal plats\nFiling of all deeds and mortgages\nMaintain records of all property owners\nCertification of tax levies for taxing districts\nCalculate tax capacity rates, credits and net property taxes\nSpecials assessments\nTransmission and Distribution Line Taxes\nMaintain ditch fund assessments\nTax increment financing\nCollection of property tax refunds\nDistribution of tax to taxing districts\nTax forfeiture proceedings\nMember of County Board of Equalization\nDeputy Registrar of Motor Vehicles\nMotor vehicle registration\nDrivers licenses, permits and ID cards\nDNR registrations of boats, snowmobiles and off-road vehicles\nGame & Fish license agent\nChief County Election Official\nVoter registration record keeping\nPrepare ballots for use in all elections in 23 county election precincts\nSecure and distribute to all precincts, supplies and equipment required\nHold training session before each election for municipal and townships clerks and election judges\nHandling of all absentee ballot requests and voting procedures\nReceive and tabulate results of elections and file these results with the Secretary of State\nMember of County Canvassing Board to check tabulations\nAssurance of election certificates to qualified election winners\nContact Us\nMon – Fri 8AM – 5PM\nRock County Facebook\nRock County YouTube\nPowered by\nVisit the Revize website (opens in a new tab)\n,\nthe Government Website Experts\nLogin\nShare this page\nShare this page\n-->\nClose\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nSource Language: Target Language: Source Text: Translated Text: Vote:\nClose Read More",
